axes.local_files:
Plugin/IDE/CLI forms work on local code; the official FAQ states that SaaS inference must pass the preceding context of the file being written to the model,
and promises (translated from the official wording) "no subsequent accumulation, analysis or processing is done with this uploaded code";
under private deployment the models and services all sit in the customer's private domain — data never leaves the domain (per the FAQ wording).

axes.background:
Mission Mode (end-to-end delivery toward an explicit goal: autonomously decomposing goals and executing until done) and Spec mode (spec-driven) both have official pages;
Automation (scheduled/event-driven automation) as an extension capability has its own page; the Comate NEXT plan (cloud workbench, autonomous agent collaboration)
is per the official docs page.

axes.tools:
Extension capabilities all have official pages: Subagent (built-in Explore subagent with its own independent context window), Skills (open-standard capability packs),
Rules (custom instructions: code standards / framework preferences / project conventions), MCP, Command, Memory;
the "@" shortcut adds File/Folder/Terminal/Doc/Rules context, the "/" shortcut adds Skills/Commands/Subagents.
